-- title:
--   Twisted stabiliser of a regular diagonal element of GL₂
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L$ a Galois extension of $K$, and let $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ be such that every $\tau \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ lies in the subgroup of integer powers of $\sigma$ (so the Galois group is cyclic, generated by $\sigma$). Let $\delta_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ be diagonal, i.e. its $(1,0)$ and $(0,1)$ entries vanish, and assume the regularity condition $N_{L/K}\bigl((\delta_0)_{00}/(\delta_0)_{11}\bigr) \neq 1$. Let $\Lambda \le \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ be a subgroup whose members are exactly those $\gamma$ with $\delta_0^{-1}\bigl(\gamma\,\delta_0\,\sigma(\gamma)^{-1}\bigr)$ in the centre of $\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$, where $\sigma(\gamma)$ denotes the entrywise application of $\sigma$ to $\gamma$, and let $\Lambda' \le \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ be a subgroup whose members are exactly those $a$ that are diagonal (vanishing $(1,0)$ and $(0,1)$ entries) and satisfy $a_{00}/a_{11} \in \mathrm{image}(K \to L)$. Then four assertions hold: $\Lambda' \le \Lambda$; every $\gamma \in \Lambda$ either lies in $\Lambda'$ or is anti-diagonal ($\gamma_{00} = \gamma_{11} = 0$) with $N_{L/K}\bigl((\delta_0)_{00}/(\delta_0)_{11}\bigr) = -1$; if $N_{L/K}\bigl((\delta_0)_{00}/(\delta_0)_{11}\bigr) = -1$ then $\Lambda$ contains an element $\gamma$ with $\gamma_{00} = \gamma_{11} = 0$; and for any $\gamma, \gamma' \in \Lambda$ with $\gamma_{00} = \gamma'_{00} = 0$ one has $\gamma^{-1}\gamma' \in \Lambda'$.
--
--   This is the computation of the $\sigma$-twisted stabiliser of a regular diagonal element of $\mathrm{GL}_2$: the conclusions say that $\Lambda$ is the union of $\Lambda'$ and, exactly when the norm of the diagonal ratio equals $-1$, a single further coset consisting of anti-diagonal elements, so that $\Lambda'$ has index $1$ or $2$ in $\Lambda$. It supplies the factor $1$ or $\tfrac12$ in the hyperbolic contributions and is used in the integrability and summability statement [`AutomorphicForm.setLIntegral_tsum_norm_bracket_mul_twistedOrbital_lt_top_and_integrableOn`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.setLIntegral_tsum_norm_bracket_mul_twistedOrbital_lt_top_and_integrableOn).
-- source:
